From 2e046a426ddf02c25fdd1a6cb194c5c9f7c596c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: letress <212964567+letress@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:42:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 55/67] phy: samsung-ufs: Add support for the Exynos9610 UFS
 PHY

Add the M-PHY settings of the Exynos9610. They are the PMA writes of the
vendor kernel's calibration tables for this SoC (ufs-cal-9610.c): the
initial settings, the ones for high speed gear 3 and the receiver
settings around hibern8. The CDR lock shows in bit 6 of register 0x7f.

The host has a single lane. The tables are laid out for a second one
0x140 bytes further on, as the vendor ones are.

The isolation of the PHY is bit 0 of the PMU register at offset 0x724.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos9610-ufs.c | 118 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c    |   3 +
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h    |   1 +
 4 files changed, 123 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos9610-ufs.c

